				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Integrate Mountain gRPC across Cocoon and synchronize Element submodules\n\nUpdate the Element submodule from ec5306a2 to 08ff6e0f, pulling in two layers of integration work: architecture detection optimization in Cocoon and the native file descriptor API in Mountain, followed by the complete wiring of Mountain gRPC across Cocoon's command synchronization, extension registry, storage persistence, and command execution event surfaces.\n\nKey modifications across components:\n- **Cocoon**: Wire MountainGRPCClientService for bidirectional command sync, merge ILocalExtension manifests from Mountain into ExtensionRegistry, replace Memento stubs with Mountain-backed persistence, and subscribe to onDidExecuteCommand events. Optimize DetectWebArchitecture with a direct synchronous process.arch check. Purge stale Target/ build artifacts.\n- **Mountain**: Implement file:open/file:close IPC backed by a process-global HashMap<u32, File>, refine Tauri window handlers (setDocumentEdited, setMinimumSize, positionWindow), eliminate polling in is_alive, reduce terminal startup latency from 120ms to 20ms and command registration yield from 50ms to 20ms. Add CustomEditorProvider registry, route watch_file/resize_terminal to real FSEvents/inotify and PTY SIGWINCH, add extensions:activate handler, introduce StorageWriteDebouncer with 100ms coalescing, strip osascript from getCursorScreenPoint, and fix logsPath in ISandboxConfiguration.\n- **Common**: Add ExtensionsActivate IPC channel mapping to complete the extension activation signal chain.\n- **Output**: Register five new channel bridges for VFS file changes, configuration updates, workspace folder changes, and lifecycle phase transitions — establishing a locked IPC contract with Wind's service layer.\n- **Wind**: Remove mock Effect.sleep(10) from MountainSyncHelper and prune hundreds of stale generated stubs and bridge shapes.\n- **Echo**: Advance to the latest development state.\n- **Documentation**: Redraw architecture diagrams across all components with detailed Mermaid subgraphs and accurate IPC flow annotations.\n\nThese changes close the last integration stubs between Cocoon and Mountain, optimize extension activation and command dispatch latency, eliminate polling overhead throughout the native backend, and align architectural documentation with the actual codebase.",
